### Description of Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The bug report indicates that the tabs component in `carbon-components-react` is not passing accessibility checks due to missing `aria-labelledby` or similar attributes on the `<button>` elements. The images show that the accessibility checker flags the `<button>` element as having no associated label.

The root cause is the lack of proper accessibility attributes (`aria-labelledby`) on the button elements within the tabs. This can prevent screen readers from correctly identifying the purpose of these buttons to users who rely on assistive technologies.

